    "bottomLine": "The glass air fryer to choose if you want more capacity and a rotisserie rather than meal-prep containers.",
    "description": "The Fritaire takes the glass idea in a different direction. A round tempered glass bowl sits under a heating head, so you see the food from every side while it cooks. Retail listings describe a 5-quart bowl, a 1,300-watt element and a maximum of 400°F, and the 9-in-1 Pro version on Amazon adds a rotisserie spit and a tumbling basket for fries and wings. The maker markets it as free of Teflon, PFAS and BPA, and it has a self-cleaning cycle: add water and a little dish soap to the bowl and run the fan. Owners commonly report that the cycle loosens light grease but does not remove baked-on stains, so expect some scrubbing. Compared with the Ninja Crispi, the Fritaire has more volume and the rotisserie option, but it lacks the storage-container trick: you cannot put a lid on the bowl and slide it into the fridge. It is also tall and round, which takes more counter space than its capacity suggests, and the listing&#39;s material list includes plastic and stainless steel parts as well as the glass. Choose it if you want to watch food crisp and you like the idea of a small rotisserie chicken on the counter. Choose the Crispi if storage and meal prep matter more than size, or if you want the higher 450°F ceiling."
